# 10. Phase 5 — Philips Hue Integration

## Objective

Deliver the first production-quality real-device integration.

Hue is the preferred first integration because it provides a strong combination of discovery, pairing, commands, events, rooms, scenes and sensors.

## P0 Deliverables

- Hue Bridge v2 discovery
- HTTPS communication
- Bridge identity validation strategy
- Link-button pairing
- Keychain credential storage
- Resource synchronization
- Event stream
- Light on/off
- Brightness
- Color temperature where supported
- Color where supported
- Grouped room control
- Reachability
- Error translation
- Diagnostics

## P1 Deliverables

- Hue rooms and zones
- Hue scene activation
- Sensors
- Buttons as events
- Gradient capability presentation
- Dynamic scene support where verified
- Route reconciliation with HomeKit-exposed Hue devices

## Rate-Limit Requirement

Ordinary REST commands must respect current verified Hue guidance.

High-frequency entertainment behavior is excluded from this phase.

## Exit Criteria

- Hue Bridge reconnects after app relaunch
- IP changes recover through stable identity and rediscovery
- Keychain contains secrets; logs and persistence do not
- Event updates refresh UI without continuous polling
- Individual and grouped commands respect rate limits
- Real hardware test matrix passes

