# 15. Phase 10 — Automation Engine

## Objective

Allow Aura to respond automatically to time and trusted local events.

## P0 Deliverables

- Time triggers
- Sunrise and sunset triggers where location permission is appropriately handled
- Hue sensor triggers
- HomeKit state triggers where supported
- Device online/offline triggers
- Conditions
- Scene actions
- Direct device actions
- Wait actions
- Conditional branches
- Cooldown
- Debounce
- Deduplication
- Loop prevention
- Execution history
- Diagnostics

## Reliability Classes

Automations should declare operational expectations such as:

- Foreground reliable
- Local event driven
- Requires Home hub
- Best effort while app is inactive
- Not supported in background

Aura must not promise continuous background execution beyond iOS capabilities.

## Exit Criteria

- Duplicate events do not cause duplicate runs
- An automation cannot recursively trigger itself without limit
- Background limitations are accurately represented
- Failed actions are recorded with recovery guidance
- Users can disable an unhealthy automation
- Automation behavior is testable with an injectable clock and event bus

